{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1054316-character-morality-versus-player-expectation","id":1054316,"title":"Character morality versus player expectation","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-24T07:58:14-08:00","id":1054316,"title":"Character morality versus player expectation","content":"A discussion sidetrack from this thread: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1051415-i-can-t-wrap-my-head-around-w-ta-help-me-get-a-clear-picture/page5\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...-picture/page5</a><br /> <br /> The reason I brought this to the general area is that the issue of characters being monsters or not vs what players want, is a very central theme in WoD. That and the thread this came from heavily discussed it.<br /> <br /> First of all, the concept of darkness in World of Darkness is not very universally agreed on and it naturally affects how the characters are seen. To some, the darkness is all encompassing and the player characters are usually monsters in some way. Another viewn is that the darkness is an overwhelming foe that needs to be pushed back. And so on.<br /> <br /> For me, the darkness isn't as much gore as it is small excuses people make or beliefs they end up with. Or the constant reminder that they are stuck.<br /> <br /> I admit one faction I have never gotten my head around is Sabbat. Their embracing of their monstrous nature is neat, but how they act and how much books press on that their bonds are false and they are simply used, puts me off.<br /> <br /> This leads to the other point I wanna discuss here, morality of a player character. To me, and I fully admit it is not a very common perspective, if I cannot look at my character and see both the honestly good and honestly bad in them I don't play them for long. By 'honestly' I mean that even if I took away tribe/clan/bloodbonds/etc., they would still have these traits because they are their core personality. I cannot just play someone who I cannot sympathize with at least a bit.<br /> <br /> But that does not mean their darkness does not matter, far from it. Most of my garou honestly do not consider humans much, they will aid them, but they frankly see only creatures that are blind to reality. A human death is not a bad thing, unless it breaks the Veil. It can even be useful in some situations. This is often in contrast to how they see feral animals, usually with a lot of respect.<br /> <br /> Then there is the whole mentality of 'yeah it sucks, but we must continue if we want to live' about Garou Nation. At times excusing outright abuse or kidnapping because it was 'just'. Hell, I remember a metis cub I played being extremely dismissive of a homesick cub, because at least no one was chaining them.<br /> <br /> Just to get this ball rolling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T08:47:21-08:00","id":1054334,"title":"","content":"But Garou are a mixture of Human, Wolf, and Spirit, so Human deaths should be avoided unless they are necessary to about a greater evil (killing hunters who are going after deer is excessive and hypocritical while killing hunter going after endangered species is permissible and encouraged). In addition, 88% of Garou are Homid, so they were raised in human societies that placed some value on Human life, and the transformation to the Garou does not wipe that slate clean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T09:09:55-08:00","id":1054344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1054316-character-morality-versus-player-expectation?p=1054334#post1054334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Garou are a mixture of Human, Wolf, and Spirit, so Human deaths should be avoided unless they are necessary to about a greater evil (killing hunters who are going after deer is excessive and hypocritical while killing hunter going after endangered species is permissible and encouraged). In addition, 88% of Garou are Homid, so they were raised in human societies that placed some value on Human life, and the transformation to the Garou does not wipe that slate clean.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I mostly play metis and lupus, so that might explain it. But on a grander scale, yeah, it is a very damn awful perspective to have. That is the point, by not seeing humans as truly that special my characters are being arseholes. They might not outwardly say it (minus one), but the speciecism is there. This does not mean all garou share this perspective, of course. Just some of my pcs who are raised in the society.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T09:42:41-08:00","id":1054348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1054316-character-morality-versus-player-expectation#post1054316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> But that does not mean their darkness does not matter, far from it. Most of my garou honestly do not consider humans much, they will aid them, but they frankly see only creatures that are blind to reality. A human death is not a bad thing, unless it breaks the Veil. It can even be useful in some situations. This is often in contrast to how they see feral animals, usually with a lot of respect.</div> </div> </div> </div>This has actually typically been my character's outlooks on humans actually. It doesn't necessarily matter if they were homid born or not. It doesn't take long to realize that an individual human life or 2 isn't terribly important in the grand scheme of things.<br /> <br /> I suppose for reference (because playing them helped shape my outlooks for characters in general), the characters I've played in long-ish (multi-year) running games were:<br /> Fianna Homid Ragabash, from Rank 2-4<br /> Silent Strider Metis Galliard, Rank 1-3<br /> Shadowlord Homid Philodox (Children of Crow camp), Rank 1-2<br /> Rokea Brightwater Squamus Rank 1-3<br /> Ratkin Metis Plague Lord Rank 1-3<br /> Rokea Dimwater Homid Rank 1-3<br /> <br /> <br /> Per the level of darkness in the world....for me, it really depends on the individual game. I've highlighted entirely different themes in different games. I do tend to enjoy having some level of real hope for positive change though. &quot;You struggle until you die horribly&quot; isn't an appealing arc for a game for me. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T09:43:38-08:00","id":1054350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1054316-character-morality-versus-player-expectation?p=1054334#post1054334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Garou are a mixture of Human, Wolf, and Spirit, so Human deaths should be avoided unless they are necessary to about a greater evil (killing hunters who are going after deer is excessive and hypocritical while killing hunter going after endangered species is permissible and encouraged). In addition, 88% of Garou are Homid, so they were raised in human societies that placed some value on Human life, and the transformation to the Garou does not wipe that slate clean.</div> </div> </div> </div>None of that explains the multiple genocides Garou have committed in the past and the new impergium they keep discussing every now and again. Garou are not americans discussing whether it's okay to kill people. Garou are nazis discussing whether they should start the Fourth Reich right now or wait a few more months.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T09:58:10-08:00","id":1054359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1054316-character-morality-versus-player-expectation?p=1054350#post1054350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">None of that explains the multiple genocides Garou have committed in the past and the new impergium they keep discussing every now and again. Garou are not americans discussing whether it's okay to kill people. Garou are nazis discussing whether they should start the Fourth Reich right now or wait a few more months.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to avoid this thread turning into another argument of this; Modern garou are not like their ancestors, they do in fact mostly try to avoid another genocide. The only tribe who truly is calling for another Impegrium is a tribe that lacks any human-born members and avoids human concepts on purpose. The rest are mostly just full of hot air.<br /> <br /> As for the genocides, they happened before humans even truly had proper culture. When a lot of humans would gladly do the same for a rivial tribe. The last one was very tied with the Spanish taking over South America. Modern garou are carrying the burden of these things, not glorifying them. And those who are are often portrayed as fools.<br /> <br /> <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona\">@idpersona </a></b><br /> Yeah, I don't like the game being lost by default.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","user":"Ana Mizuki","date":". 02-24-2017, 01:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T11:32:27-08:00","id":1054386,"title":"","content":"Well, I think that the key thing to remember about WtA is that there is no inevitable end game, there is just the inevitability of the corruption of everything if they do not fight the Wyrm and the stasis of everything if they do not fight the Weaver. The Fera are powerful creatures, beginning Fera are generally the most powerful beginning characters in cWoD, and they are capable of accomplishing great things, though more in the vein of 'epic deeds' rather than in the vein of 'good deeds'. That being said, the majority of the Fera understand that most of them will die in the pursuit of great things but, as long as the goal is accomplished, I do not think that they would blink at accepting ninety percent casualty rates as long as their Human Kinfolk and Animal Kinfolk survive (with the exception of the Corax, as their reproduction is expensive).<br /> <br /> Among the Garou, the tendency towards meaningful self-sacrifice is exaggerated even more because they are born to be the warriors of Gaia. The White Howlers sacrificed their entire Tribe in a vain attempt to destroy the Wyrm, and they paid the price by becoming the Black Spiral Dancers. The Croatan sacrificed their entire Tribe in a successful attempt to banish the Eater-of-Souls, and they disappeared from the Earth. The Garou are willing to die to protect Gaia and, as long as they can take out a few hundred foes in the process, they will die happy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T11:44:16-08:00","id":1054392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1054316-character-morality-versus-player-expectation?p=1054350#post1054350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">None of that explains the multiple genocides Garou have committed in the past and the new impergium they keep discussing every now and again</div> </div> </div> </div>The only &quot;new Impergiums&quot; they talk about is the one they know can't be put into place, or the comparison of how humans treat wolves. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Garou are nazis discussing whether they should start the Fourth Reich right now or wait a few more months. </div> </div> </div>Only the Swords of Heimdall, and if you're running back onto a metaplot timeline following Revised, they're basically dead and probably trying to find a place less obvious than South America to hide (particularly because the Amazon War is winding down and any new Garou arriving in South America are going to get it from both the Garou Nation and the native Fera if they try anything).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T12:27:35-08:00","id":1054409,"title":"","content":"For Mages, in game they're supposed to start with moralities similar to that of normal people, that change when they enter in contact with the alien moralities and realities of the Traditons and the Technocracy. Mages *know* that the world it's different from what they knew in their past live, and this difference necessarily has to impact in the value of human life and such. Among other things this encourages &quot;blue and orange moralities&quot;. I.E: The value of free will probably changes when you can see the world as The Merovingian from Matrix","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T12:48:32-08:00","id":1054424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1054316-character-morality-versus-player-expectation#post1054316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I admit one faction I have never gotten my head around is Sabbat. Their embracing of their monstrous nature is neat, but how they act and how much books press on that their bonds are false and they are simply used, puts me off.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing about the Sabbat is that they sell you on freedom from elder control or human morality and then immediately enslave you into a blood bonded suicide squad. The Sabbat exist as a foil against the Camarilla - the illusion of freedom superimposed over a much deeper slavery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T12:55:54-08:00","id":1054428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1054316-character-morality-versus-player-expectation?p=1054409#post1054409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Mages, in game they're supposed to start with moralities similar to that of normal people, that change when they enter in contact with the alien moralities and realities of the Traditons and the Technocracy. Mages *know* that the world it's different from what they knew in their past live, and this difference necessarily has to impact in the value of human life and such. Among other things this encourages &quot;blue and orange moralities&quot;. I.E: The value of free will probably changes when you can see the world as The Merovingian from Matrix</div> </div> </div> </div>Mages are people of <b>Hubris</b>. They are still humans however, so they are NOT automatically alien monsters; they are, however, the pinnacle of the human kind.<br /> <br /> And they know it.<br /> <br /> Even the most pious Chorister, or the most wise and humble Akashic, <b>knows</b> that they are <b>above those pitiful sleepers</b><br /> <br /> Even the way they describe the mundanes - sleepers - as opposed to the title of &quot;awakened&quot; that they have for themselves shows how Mages/Scientists see themselves as superior to the &quot;masses&quot;.<br /> <br /> In time, those &quot;masses&quot; of people become mere numbers... Sleepers don't know what's good for them, but <i>You do!</i>.<br /> <br /> Sleepers must worship God;<br /> Sleepers must serve the spirits;<br /> Sleepers must keep the Wheel;<br /> Sleepers must adhere to Science.<br /> <br /> That's how I like to play Mage, no matter if with the Union or with the Traditions.<br /> <br /> He can have the best intentions in the world, it may wanna the uttermost good<br /> <br /> But, by the end of the day, Mages are all fascists at heart. Well, it's hard not being one when you can control reality itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12880,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","user":"Karlgust","date":". 02-24-2017, 04:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T13:00:30-08:00","id":1054431,"title":"","content":"Wraiths are like Doctor Jekill and Mister Hyde... All the time. I say that they are even worse than vampires","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T13:03:47-08:00","id":1054432,"title":"","content":"Changellings maybe are the one rain of light on WoD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T13:05:43-08:00","id":1054434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1054316-character-morality-versus-player-expectation?p=1054424#post1054424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing about the Sabbat is that they sell you on freedom from elder control or human morality and then immediately enslave you into a blood bonded suicide squad. The Sabbat exist as a foil against the Camarilla - the illusion of freedom superimposed over a much deeper slavery.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that is the other part. They act like frat boys on crack (yes, I know not all do) and that alone grates me a bit. But the slavery on top of it basically makes me roll my eyes. I'm not saying they are unplayable, but not for me sadly ^^''","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T14:10:49-08:00","id":1054460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1054316-character-morality-versus-player-expectation?p=1054434#post1054434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And that is the other part. They act like frat boys on crack (yes, I know not all do) and that alone grates me a bit. But the slavery on top of it basically makes me roll my eyes. I'm not saying they are unplayable, but not for me sadly ^^''</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Don't get me wrong, the Sabbat are a hooooot mess. But I believe that stems more from too many cooks spoiling the borth, or more locally some players seeing the Sabbat as license to enact their darkest absurdist murder fantasies or just use it as a way to add crossover elements to VtM.<br /> <br /> Because, and correct me if I'm wrong, the Sabbat were originally intended to be a shadowy organization that may or may not exist. There was little to no information about them, what there was often contradicted itself, and ultimately their form or purpose was entirely up to the ST's control. The only single unifying thread was that they were an organization of inhuman vampires. And that was taken many different ways. <br /> <br /> Then the game world grew smaller, the blank parts of the map were filled up, and the Sabbat needed more concrete organization and purpose within the setting. And the designers said: &quot;Hey, why not make it an organization where all of the possible iterations could potentially be right.&quot;<br /> <br /> And thus the hot mess that is the Sabbat is born, welcoming all possible iterations so long as they drink the blood, oppose the Camarilla, pay lip service to the majority faction's Noddist roots, and actively all agree Infernalism is one step too far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T14:42:48-08:00","id":1054470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changellings maybe are the one rain of light on WoD</div> </div> </div> </div>Seelie Changellings maybe, perhaps, sometimes, when they're in a good mood. Unseelie on the other hand...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T15:14:23-08:00","id":1054477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1054316-character-morality-versus-player-expectation?p=1054470#post1054470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Seelie Changellings maybe, perhaps, sometimes, when they're in a good mood. Unseelie on the other hand...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeahh, Kithain are pretty much on the same level of inhuman as the garou are. I mean, let us look at the sidhe and what they did when commers didn't just bow to them. Or Redcaps in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T15:31:49-08:00","id":1054482,"title":"","content":"Yes, and they get even stranger the longer they spend in the Dreaming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T15:43:15-08:00","id":1054488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1054316-character-morality-versus-player-expectation?p=1054392#post1054392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The only &quot;new Impergiums&quot; they talk about is the one they know can't be put into place, or the comparison of how humans treat wolves.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Only the Swords of Heimdall, and if you're running back onto a metaplot timeline following Revised, they're basically dead and probably trying to find a place less obvious than South America to hide (particularly because the Amazon War is winding down and any new Garou arriving in South America are going to get it from both the Garou Nation and the native Fera if they try anything).</div> </div> </div> </div>From the latest interview with Martin Ericsson:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And in between all of that you have all of the other tribes who have their own ideas about how to deal with humanity and what we\u2019ve done wrong. The Black Furies are a matriarchal clan who don\u2019t want to help the humans until they sort out their gender rights, <b>The Get of Fenris who just laugh at all of those social aims and say it\u2019s about survival of the fittest, and they should go into all-out war to see if humans can survive.</b> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T15:46:18-08:00","id":1054489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1054316-character-morality-versus-player-expectation?p=1054460#post1054460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, the Sabbat are a hooooot mess. But I believe that stems more from too many cooks spoiling the borth, or more locally some players seeing the Sabbat as license to enact their darkest absurdist murder fantasies or just use it as a way to add crossover elements to VtM.<br /> <br /> Because, and correct me if I'm wrong, the Sabbat were originally intended to be a shadowy organization that may or may not exist. There was little to no information about them, what there was often contradicted itself, and ultimately their form or purpose was entirely up to the ST's control. The only single unifying thread was that they were an organization of inhuman vampires. And that was taken many different ways.<br /> <br /> Then the game world grew smaller, the blank parts of the map were filled up, and the Sabbat needed more concrete organization and purpose within the setting. And the designers said: &quot;Hey, why not make it an organization where all of the possible iterations could potentially be right.&quot;<br /> <br /> And thus the hot mess that is the Sabbat is born, welcoming all possible iterations so long as they drink the blood, oppose the Camarilla, pay lip service to the majority faction's Noddist roots, and actively all agree Infernalism is one step too far.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sabbat had been all sorts of impossible things, including being the go to Infernalist faction. As well as the fuck masquerade run with a burning chainsaw and have an orgy faction. As well as anarcho-communist atheist faction. As well as the hardcore christian faction. There's basically no coherent picture of what the Sabbat is and what they want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T16:33:37-08:00","id":1054502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1054316-character-morality-versus-player-expectation?p=1054488#post1054488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> From the latest interview with Martin Ericsson:</div> </div> </div> </div>Well looks like they might take Werewolf in a similar unappealing direction as Vampire 5th. Guess we'll see.<br /> That statement seems to contradict how both of those Tribes were expended on in Revised.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T18:13:49-08:00","id":1054557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1054316-character-morality-versus-player-expectation?p=1054502#post1054502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well looks like they might take Werewolf in a similar unappealing direction as Vampire 5th. Guess we'll see.<br /> That statement seems to contradict how both of those Tribes were expended on in Revised.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a bit stronger than &quot;seems to contradict&quot;, I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T18:17:12-08:00","id":1054560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1054316-character-morality-versus-player-expectation?p=1054557#post1054557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That's a bit stronger than &quot;seems to contradict&quot;, I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm trying to be as optimistic as I can in regards that quote. It really isn't encouraging.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T19:10:16-08:00","id":1054584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1054316-character-morality-versus-player-expectation?p=1054428#post1054428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mages are people of <b>Hubris</b>. They are still humans however, so they are NOT automatically alien monsters; they are, however, the pinnacle of the human kind.<br /> <br /> And they know it.<br /> <br /> Even the most pious Chorister, or the most wise and humble Akashic, <b>knows</b> that they are <b>above those pitiful sleepers</b><br /> <br /> Even the way they describe the mundanes - sleepers - as opposed to the title of &quot;awakened&quot; that they have for themselves shows how Mages/Scientists see themselves as superior to the &quot;masses&quot;.<br /> <br /> In time, those &quot;masses&quot; of people become mere numbers... Sleepers don't know what's good for them, but <i>You do!</i>.<br /> <br /> Sleepers must worship God;<br /> Sleepers must serve the spirits;<br /> Sleepers must keep the Wheel;<br /> Sleepers must adhere to Science.<br /> <br /> That's how I like to play Mage, no matter if with the Union or with the Traditions.<br /> <br /> He can have the best intentions in the world, it may wanna the uttermost good<br /> <br /> But, by the end of the day, Mages are all fascists at heart. Well, it's hard not being one when you can control reality itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am the opposite, all my mage character dont care about the consensus, the ascension war or moving the masses. Maybe its because i started with revised when the war was lost and nobody cared about it but to me mages are just people with magic, not a race on their own with the whole sleeper/awakened thing. The whole control reality itself is more of a OOC knowledge that the typical mage shouldnt know, he just knows that his belief/practices give him access to certain kind of magic. I always move away from the whole Matrix analogy for both mages.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1054316-character-morality-versus-player-expectation?p=1054488#post1054488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the latest interview with Martin Ericsson:</div> </div> </div> </div>Dammit Dracula, this is why we cant have nice things <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As for the darkness in WoD, i always saw it as an external thing as DM. Your environment is the one that push you toward the darkness and is your inner self the one who has the potential to embrace or fight it (i have however never cared to DM vampire, so there is that) however something I always try to avoid are the cosmic anvils. Its something that i pick from bad CoC games in which no matter what your character does, how smart he is or what decisions he makes at the end of the story he cant be happy. Either he is dead, jaded or crazy because thats how lovecraft works and its the &quot;point&quot; of the setting.<br /> <br /> Same with wod i have being in many games in which the DM would just make &quot;fate&quot; destroy any happiness your character has achieve for angts and because thats the point of WoD. And its something i strongly disagree, for darkness to have any meaning you need light. If there is a ways for everything to go horribly wrong there has to be a ways to get your cake and eat it too. Of course in logical plausible way, you arent gonna single handily destroy the wyrm and noone is gonna die but still.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 02-24-2017, 10:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T21:01:30-08:00","id":1054627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1054316-character-morality-versus-player-expectation?p=1054488#post1054488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the latest interview with Martin Ericsson:<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>...I just.... buh?<br /> <br /> Garou are not vampires, people. Like, they literally -cannot- function without their human kinfolk support network. Which usually consists of humans they are related to in some way. Unless there was a HUGE surge of wolves, both Furies AND Fenrir gotta give ALL the craps.<br /> <br /> This is not directed at you, Kammerer. Just the quote you put there makes me groan.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T22:24:55-08:00","id":1054651,"title":"","content":"Well, just another reason to be skeptical of a 5th edition. First, Shadowun, now cWoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T03:36:46-08:00","id":1054697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1054316-character-morality-versus-player-expectation?p=1054651#post1054651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, just another reason to be skeptical of a 5th edition. First, Shadowun, now cWoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is honestly pretty bad, in the terms of this thread even.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat, even though they are edgy and stuff, are that way for a reason.<br /> <br /> The text above about Furies and the Fenrir? It is just them being edgy and SO AWFUL because THEY don't care about your safe places and triggers! As in, the darkness is baked in by force, not coming through naturally from the setting itself. Especially with Black Furies who basically are the most vocal people about women's rights, they WOULD care about these things. And Fenrir respect strength in all its forms, so they would also respect those who rise against tyranny even though disadvantaged.<br /> <br /> Of course, each character is an induvidual, so variety exists.<br /> <br /> Though, if we go by MET and list the -jobs- these guys do, I'll have to look for my eyes since they rolled so hard they fell off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T06:56:51-08:00","id":1054735,"title":"","content":"Well, at least we will have the previous editions to fall back on (including the 20th editions created by Onyx Path). I am not that worried about 5e frankly because Paradox will bankrupt itself trying to create video games based off cWoD. I would be more worried if a large company like EA had bought the rights because they are large enough to survive a few bad releases before they figured out a popular model for cWoD games (and would have destroyed the memories of our youth in the process).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T09:45:48-08:00","id":1054810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1054316-character-morality-versus-player-expectation?p=1054460#post1054460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, the Sabbat are a hooooot mess. But I believe that stems more from too many cooks spoiling the borth, or more locally some players seeing the Sabbat as license to enact their darkest absurdist murder fantasies or just use it as a way to add crossover elements to VtM.<br /> <br /> Because, and correct me if I'm wrong, the Sabbat were originally intended to be a shadowy organization that may or may not exist. There was little to no information about them, what there was often contradicted itself, and ultimately their form or purpose was entirely up to the ST's control. The only single unifying thread was that they were an organization of inhuman vampires. And that was taken many different ways. <br /> <br /> Then the game world grew smaller, the blank parts of the map were filled up, and the Sabbat needed more concrete organization and purpose within the setting. And the designers said: &amp;quot;Hey, why not make it an organization where all of the possible iterations could potentially be right.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> And thus the hot mess that is the Sabbat is born, welcoming all possible iterations so long as they drink the blood, oppose the Camarilla, pay lip service to the majority faction's Noddist roots, and actively all agree Infernalism is one step too far.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, the good old days were you could choose ONLY between 7 clans of the Camarilla, the most &quot;weird&quot; unique disciplines were metamorphosis and thaumaturgy, and ANY power beyond 5 were a total mystery... Good times indeed, were no player would argue with you to say &quot;no way a 8th generation Tzimisce can do that, look here at Vivisscitute! It doesn't have that power!&quot;.<br /> <br /> That's why the two clans of the Sabbat are the Tzimisce and Lasombra: it was to have two monstruous powers (vicissitude and obtenabration), because they were meant to be antagonists. <br /> <br /> But, the Sabbat became a Circus the moment it were better depicted...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T09:55:23-08:00","id":1054814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1054316-character-morality-versus-player-expectation?p=1054584#post1054584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am the opposite, all my mage character dont care about the consensus, the ascension war or moving the masses. Maybe its because i started with revised when the war was lost and nobody cared about it but to me mages are just people with magic, not a race on their own with the whole sleeper/awakened thing. The whole control reality itself is more of a OOC knowledge that the typical mage shouldnt know, he just knows that his belief/practices give him access to certain kind of magic. I always move away from the whole Matrix analogy for both mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>It may be. However, you still knows that you're better than those &quot;deluded fools&quot; you call as sleepers. And the best emotion that you can feel about sleepers is <i>piety</i> - which isn't a very good compliment to them (that's also the reason that Hubris Mages will get so much awe for when a sleeper make an invention or show some skill the Mage would never think a sleeper could possess)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1054316-character-morality-versus-player-expectation?p=1054584#post1054584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dammit Dracula, this is why we cant have nice things <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As for the darkness in WoD, i always saw it as an external thing as DM. Your environment is the one that push you toward the darkness and is your inner self the one who has the potential to embrace or fight it (i have however never cared to DM vampire, so there is that) however something I always try to avoid are the cosmic anvils. Its something that i pick from bad CoC games in which no matter what your character does, how smart he is or what decisions he makes at the end of the story he cant be happy. Either he is dead, jaded or crazy because thats how lovecraft works and its the &amp;quot;point&amp;quot; of the setting.<br /> <br /> Same with wod i have being in many games in which the DM would just make &amp;quot;fate&amp;quot; destroy any happiness your character has achieve for angts and because thats the point of WoD. And its something i strongly disagree, for darkness to have any meaning you need light. If there is a ways for everything to go horribly wrong there has to be a ways to get your cake and eat it too. Of course in logical plausible way, you arent gonna single handily destroy the wyrm and noone is gonna die but still.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, I guess Vampire, but most of all, Wraith, aren't for you.<br /> <br /> Mage, Werewolf and Changelling, however, are probably more to your liking","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T10:09:23-08:00","id":1054821,"title":"","content":"About a new Impergium... Yeah, it would be funny to think about 20-40 thousands of Fera declaring a &quot;all-out war&quot; against 7 BILLIONS of human beings... Im not even going to talk about what the Technocracy or some 40-60 thousands kindred may think of this, since we can disregard those in a pure werewolf game, but need I remember you that the Garou nation can't even defeat the Pentex? Now, just imagine all the executives of Pentex approaching the world governaments to give their &quot;consultant services&quot;... And, basically, placing the full mighty of the US, Europe, Russia and China militaries (and many many others) at their disposal in order to deal with those &quot;mutants&quot; (apache's choppers and intelligent missile cruisers at your Caern aint pretty).<br /> <br /> Declaring war on humanity is the most stupid decision that ANY splat could do (and lets not forget, humans can and WILL resort to nukes if they are too hard pressed).<br /> <br /> And, for WtA in part\u00edcular, that would be the fastest way to ensure the wyrm's final victory","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T11:21:53-08:00","id":1054879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1054316-character-morality-versus-player-expectation?p=1054821#post1054821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About a new Impergium... Yeah, it would be funny to think about 20-40 thousands of Fera declaring a &quot;all-out war&quot; against 7 BILLIONS of human beings... Im not even going to talk about what the Technocracy or some 40-60 thousands kindred may think of this, since we can disregard those in a pure werewolf game, but need I remember you that the Garou nation can't even defeat the Pentex? Now, just imagine all the executives of Pentex approaching the world governaments to give their &quot;consultant services&quot;... And, basically, placing the full mighty of the US, Europe, Russia and China militaries (and many many others) at their disposal in order to deal with those &quot;mutants&quot; (apache's choppers and intelligent missile cruisers at your Caern aint pretty).<br /> <br /> Declaring war on humanity is the most stupid decision that ANY splat could do (and lets not forget, humans can and WILL resort to nukes if they are too hard pressed).<br /> <br /> And, for WtA in part\u00edcular, that would be the fastest way to ensure the wyrm's final victory</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't entirely true. Look at some the Apocalypse scenarios. Meteor hit or worldwide earthquake are both valid (and arguably Gaian) ways to decimate humanity.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T12:49:25-08:00","id":1054918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1054316-character-morality-versus-player-expectation?p=1054814#post1054814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It may be. However, you still knows that you're better than those &quot;deluded fools&quot; you call as sleepers. And the best emotion that you can feel about sleepers is <i>piety</i> - which isn't a very good compliment to them (that's also the reason that Hubris Mages will get so much awe for when a sleeper make an invention or show some skill the Mage would never think a sleeper could possess)</div> </div> </div> </div>Uhm not really how i play it. Is like mutant powers some people have them some people dont and they manage to live perfectly good lives without it. I just dont like that particular aspect of Ascension, the whole &quot;being a mage makes you superior to human on a cosmological level&quot; when most of the time you still a human that can fart a fireball is you follow a set of rules. Any sleeper can learn sorcery and in the games i have played/run there is not really a division between Magic and Magick. The whole &quot;magic is this thing that makes you superior to humans understanding&quot; is frankly lost on me, i prefer the &quot;you got magic powers because of your practices, what you do with it is up to you&quot; but removing the &quot;meddling with sleeper society&quot; aspect of it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1054316-character-morality-versus-player-expectation?p=1054814#post1054814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I guess Vampire, but most of all, Wraith, aren't for you.<br /> <br /> Mage, Werewolf and Changelling, however, are probably more to your liking</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a particular relationship with Masquerade, i can play it as long as i can just ignore the whole personal horror angle and focus on occultism with fangs with all the fun sorceries and secrets. However i do like Requiem because it just takes the element i have most problem in Masquerade (what do you do?) and makes it central part of the game. I enjoy the lore and setting but not much the game itself.<br /> <br /> Wraith though, i heard is a nightmare to run and its premise is simple not attractive to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 02-25-2017, 05:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T14:26:07-08:00","id":1054940,"title":"","content":"Well, the Fera are more the equivalent of around 75,000 to 150,000 members depending on the interpretation of the Lore and are really, really scary for normal humans to face. Something on the order of 86% of normal humans will run screaming from Fera and then forget about everything in a few minutes while another 7% will run screaming and will rationalize the event as a bear attack or a serial killer in a wolf mask, so it is nearly impossible for military units to withstand Fera attacks because they will dissolve in panic. When you combine that with superhuman attributes, magical Gifts, and Umbra travel, things get bad for normal humans really quickly. While it would be difficult for Fera to infiltrate level 4 biological facilities, it is not impossible, and strategically spreading ebola, smallpox, etc could kill off 50% of humanity before any government understands they are under coordinated attack. If the Fera are willing to risk Wyrm contamination, they can just summon the spirits of the diseases and spread them without mundane vectors. Fortunately, the Fera understand that mass genocide only strengthens the Wyrm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T01:27:40-08:00","id":1055132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1054316-character-morality-versus-player-expectation?p=1054697#post1054697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The text above about Furies and the Fenrir? It is just them being edgy and SO AWFUL because THEY don't care about your safe places and triggers! As in, the darkness is baked in by force, not coming through naturally from the setting itself. Especially with Black Furies who basically are the most vocal people about women's rights, they WOULD care about these things.</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I remember of the Black Furies splatbook, they were mostly on the side of #KillAllMen type of feminism with the original Black Furies killing all male offspring and the modern Black Furies having a serial killer The Manslayer who acts with a backing of the Black Furies counsil.<br /> It's actually rather weird that Black Furies now also care about transgender rights rather than declaring them a wyrmish abomination and calling it a day. I know, representation and all, but Garou as written are really not the camp I see holding the torch of progressivism. They are exactly the opposite of progressivism, being anti-technology, anti-urbanism and anti-civilization.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T01:42:14-08:00","id":1055135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1054316-character-morality-versus-player-expectation?p=1054879#post1054879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This isn't entirely true. Look at some the Apocalypse scenarios. Meteor hit or worldwide earthquake are both valid (and arguably Gaian) ways to decimate humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. I forgot about the spirit world. Guess it would only be up to other supernaturals to intervene than.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T02:01:49-08:00","id":1055138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1054316-character-morality-versus-player-expectation?p=1054940#post1054940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the Fera are more the equivalent of around 75,000 to 150,000 members depending on the interpretation of the Lore and are really, really scary for normal humans to face. Something on the order of 86% of normal humans will run screaming from Fera and then forget about everything in a few minutes while another 7% will run screaming and will rationalize the event as a bear attack or a serial killer in a wolf mask, so it is nearly impossible for military units to withstand Fera attacks because they will dissolve in panic. When you combine that with superhuman attributes, magical Gifts, and Umbra travel, things get bad for normal humans really quickly. While it would be difficult for Fera to infiltrate level 4 biological facilities, it is not impossible, and strategically spreading ebola, smallpox, etc could kill off 50% of humanity before any government understands they are under coordinated attack. If the Fera are willing to risk Wyrm contamination, they can just summon the spirits of the diseases and spread them without mundane vectors. Fortunately, the Fera understand that mass genocide only strengthens the Wyrm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, and them the Pentex would &quot;save&quot; the day.<br /> <br /> And the scared humans would drop several nukes in an attempt to deal with the problem, guided by pentex &quot;adivisors&quot;. One nuke for every single Caern in the world, that should do (Pemtex would say).<br /> <br /> As for &quot;running in fear&quot;, 0.5% of the population with 10 willpower is 35 millions of people. That's a lot, and those would be recruited. Besides, the Delirium wouldn't play out from a supersonic jet, or on a screen from a guided missile. Or from a drone.<br /> As for the diseases... Yeah, it could cause massive deaths. But wouldn't kill all humans. And they would be able to fight back.<br /> And again, nukes. The humans would destroy the world with nukes, and than the Fera would have a Pirric victory. That would be, indeed, the Apocalypse.<br /> <br /> And all that goes without considering other supernaturals, considering a game of Fera exclusevily with them. If you add Technocrats/Traditionalists (that CAN remove much of the Umbral advantage of the Fera) and all vampires, changellings, even wraiths... Things get more messy.<br /> <br /> Not to mention that all Nefandi/Shadow Court/Baali would probably ally with Pentex for their &quot;final hour&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T03:39:13-08:00","id":1055159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1054316-character-morality-versus-player-expectation?p=1055132#post1055132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what I remember of the Black Furies splatbook, they were mostly on the side of #KillAllMen type of feminism with the original Black Furies killing all male offspring and the modern Black Furies having a serial killer The Manslayer who acts with a backing of the Black Furies counsil.<br /> It's actually rather weird that Black Furies now also care about transgender rights rather than declaring them a wyrmish abomination and calling it a day. I know, representation and all, but Garou as written are really not the camp I see holding the torch of progressivism. They are exactly the opposite of progressivism, being anti-technology, anti-urbanism and anti-civilization.</div> </div> </div> </div>What edition book? 1st ed or Revised?<br /> <br /> Also, garou -need- humans to continue their lineage, as most die before the age of 40. And most homid garou grow up in the human world, so these issues would be in their minds easily.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T08:13:03-08:00","id":1055246,"title":"","content":"I agree, Fera need humans, especially Human Kinfolk. In my games, Human Kinfolk are cherished and protected and, while they might be considered to be inadequate warriors, they are encouraged to pursue their own talents, so they are respected among the Garou for being everything from accountants to zoologists. In many of my WtA games, it is the Human Kinfolk who protect the Animal Kinfolk from hunters and it is the Human Kinfolk who report the concerning events to their Garou Kin that lead to campaigns.<br /> <br /> For example, in one of my games, a Human Kinfolk social worker, one of the Human Kinfolk sisters of the Lupus Garou of the group (their father played both sides of the fence), reported that one of the girls in her files had recently disappeared and asked her Lupus brother to look into things for her. The PCs agree and the quest led them to a white slavery ring run by the Russian Mafia. When they rescued the girl (and a few dozen other girls), they found records that led them to a network of child brothels throughout the NY metropolitan area that the Russian Mafia supplied. When they started raiding the child brothels, they ran into the Seventh Generation and found evidence linking the child brothels to a specific financial firm (which was a subsidiary of Pentex). <br /> <br /> By the time they were finished, they managed to cost Pentex over $100 billion by accessing and diverting the accounts of that financial firm through the shell companies they had stolen from the Russian Mafia and into environmental and social non-profits controlled by Human Kinfolk (keeping 10% for thmselves). It was a successful campaign that harmed Pentex greatly, weakened the Wyrm by rescuing children from violation and by killing the men who violated children, and by funding hundreds of non-profits which sought to preserve Gaia by educating humans and saving animals. Yes, the Garou butchered a lot of humans, but I doubt that any player wept a single tear when they slaughtered the customers of the child brothels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T10:16:22-08:00","id":1055302,"title":"","content":"$100 billions? Do you have any idea of how many companies have that kind of money in the real world?<br /> <br /> After that huge financial blow, the Pentex would be no more...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T11:27:01-08:00","id":1055321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1054316-character-morality-versus-player-expectation?p=1055302#post1055302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After that huge financial blow, the Pentex would be <s>no more...</s>bailed out by the Federal Government.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> FTFY. .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T12:09:15-08:00","id":1055338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1054316-character-morality-versus-player-expectation?p=1055132#post1055132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what I remember of the Black Furies splatbook, they were mostly on the side of #KillAllMen type of feminism with the original Black Furies killing all male offspring</div> </div> </div> </div>Then you need to read it again, because those things aren't in there. &quot;Black Furies kill male offspring!&quot; is a 1e-ism, noted in an essay from the first player's guide and promptly, it seems, forgotten afterward.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and the modern Black Furies having a serial killer The Manslayer who acts with a backing of the Black Furies counsil. </div> </div> </div>You really don't remember well at all, then, because that character is an enigma who suits the purposes of only one person, the Storyteller of your game. The only thing offered about this character is a bunch of rumormill and speculation about who she could be. The only suggestions about a network of support for said character involve an alliance of various different tribal camps or a small group of extremist Furies, per the words of the text itself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's actually rather weird that Black Furies now also care about transgender rights rather than declaring them a wyrmish abomination and calling it a day. I know, representation and all, but Garou as written are really not the camp I see holding the torch of progressivism. They are exactly the opposite of progressivism, being anti-technology, anti-urbanism and anti-civilization. </div> </div> </div>They're a very particular form of &quot;conservative&quot; that doesn't hold the same values as modern conservative party members even in part. They're going to be 100% behind some things that the American right would utterly abhor, like de-criminalizing sex work and protecting sex workers. They're going to want people to not multiply carelessly or grow in population, much like most Garou. They aren't going to have any truck with a lot of the more modern doctrines of hate, such as racism. They might ascribe overly much symbolic or spiritual mean with transgender folk, but they aren't going to look askance at them, because they would have been living with them since there were humans. That's how old their &quot;conservative&quot; bent is - and do recall, they also revere change, since they take the embattled Wyld's side when the Triat starts causing a fuss, so they actually are about various forms of progressivism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T13:36:46-08:00","id":1055369,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it is generally better to think that the Black Furies oppose everything that modern Conservatives cherish and value.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Ay